  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p>Last updated: November 15, 2026</p>

  <h2>1. About PeakReplay Clips</h2>
  <p>
    PeakReplay Clips is a desktop-based video preparation tool
    currently in development. It is intended to help creators
    prepare short-form videos and use authorized social media
    integrations.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Information We May Process</h2>
  <p>
    If social media integrations are enabled, the application
    may process account identifiers, authorization tokens,
    video files, captions, and publishing-related metadata
    necessary to provide its functionality.
  </p>

  <h2>3. How Information Is Used</h2>
  <p>
    Information is used to authenticate authorized accounts,
    prepare video content, and perform actions explicitly
    requested by the account holder.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Data Storage and Security</h2>
  <p>
    The current development version runs locally on the
    developer's computer. Future versions may use additional
    infrastructure, in which case this policy will be updated
    before those features become available.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Data Sharing</h2>
  <p>
    Information may be transmitted to connected social media
    platforms when users authorize the integration and
    initiate supported actions. We do not sell personal data.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Data Retention and Deletion</h2>
  <p>
    Account authorization information and locally stored
    content may be retained as necessary for the application's
    functionality. Users may request deletion of their data
    using the contact information provided by the application.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Changes to This Policy</h2>
  <p>
    This policy may be updated as the application develops.
    The latest version will be available on this website.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    For privacy questions or data deletion requests, please
    contact the application operator through the contact
    information published on the PeakReplay Clips website.
  </p>
